<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/claim/morphoeval-douady-magnetic-drop-phyllotaxis> a pk1:Claim ;
    rdfs:label "Douady & Couder (1992, 1996) self-organized magnetic-drop phyllotaxis & imperfect pitchfork cascade (Pinus sp. conifer seed cone & botanical shoot apical meristem (SAM))",
        "Douady & Couder (1992, 1996) self-organized magnetic-drop phyllotaxis & imperfect pitchfork cascade faithfully reproduces Pinus sp. conifer seed cone & botanical shoot apical meristem (SAM) morphology" ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/douady-magnetic-drop-phyllotaxis-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/douady-magnetic-drop-phyllotaxis-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/douady-magnetic-drop-phyllotaxis-3>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/douady-magnetic-drop-phyllotaxis-4>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/douady-magnetic-drop-phyllotaxis-5> ;
    dct:description "The simulation script(s) 1992-douady-magnetic-drop-phyllotaxis.py implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Pinus sp. conifer seed cone & botanical shoot apical meristem (SAM) specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is the weight of evidence (MorphoEval 0.1.0 overall 90.2/100, audit 2026-10-19-magnetic-drop-phyllotaxis-audit-v3) and the assessments." ;
    dct:subject <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/1992-douady-magnetic-drop-phyllotaxis.py> ;
    schema:about "Pinus sp. conifer seed cone & botanical shoot apical meristem (SAM)" ;
    schema:additionalProperty "does_not_claim: Subcellular PIN1 polar auxin efflux carrier trafficking or continuous reaction-diffusion PDE dynamics on the meristem (Slot 033 Jönsson et al. 2006 / Smith et al. 2006); 3D photogrammetric or micro-CT cone reconstruction (the specimen analysis is a single 2D apical photograph of a 3D cone); a scale-level segmentation of the cone (the DoG detections over-count by ~2x and are not used at lattice level)",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Exact static Hessian fold (G_fold = 0.773484 exp / 2.514560 lin) AND dynamical pitchfork (G_c1 = 0.859019 exp full chain / 3.631432 lin 2-drop) roots, the EMERGENT threshold of the unclamped iterated map (G_c1^emp = 0.8595 by bisection), the regular-spiral zero-force locus F(G, dphi) = 0, and adiabatic continuation along both Fibonacci (r = 0.99999, RMSE = 0.065 deg, contact pairs 9/10 table rows) and Lucas (RMSE = 0.141 deg) branches",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Nearest-neighbour contact parastichy pairs on the true radii r_k = exp(kG) (Delaunay census kept as a secondary, biased extractor), memory-depth sweep N_mem in {1,2,3,5,8,13,21,45}, gamma in {1,3,5} universality, and simulated divergence / pair at the six tabulated dish regimes (RMSE 0.141 deg, 6/6 pairs)",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Reciprocal-lattice inversion m*alpha + omega_m*G = 2*pi*j_m of the sub-bin (5, 8) log-polar FFT peaks of `conifer_cone_specimen.jpg` giving alpha_emp = 138.03 deg and G_emp = 0.0308, validated on a synthetic log-polar image of the simulated G = 0.06 lattice (0.014 deg / 0.06 % recovery error)",
        "reported_in_source: Douady & Couder (1992) Fig. 3 & (1996) J. Theor. Biol. 178:255-274 Secs. 3-4: supercritical (1,1)->(1,2) pitchfork of the iterated map, imperfect pitchfork cascade along the Fibonacci branch -> 137.508 deg, disconnected Lucas branch -> 99.502 deg, and nearest-neighbour contact parastichies on the van Iterson lattice",
        "reported_in_source: Douady & Couder (1992) Phys. Rev. Lett. 68:2098-2101 iterative magnetic-dipole repulsion energy E(phi) = sum_{k>=1} d_k(phi, phi_{n-k})^{-3} on a circular rim r = R_0 with linear dish advection r_k = R_0(1 + kG) controlled by the plastochron ratio G = V T / R_0; Figs. 1-2 dish regimes (1,1), (2,3), (3,5), (5,8), (8,13) and a metastable Lucas (4,7)",
        "transfer_boundary: Exponential meristem advection r_k = R_0 exp(kG) is displayed in the log-radial projection rho = 1 + ln(r/R_0) = 1 + kG, which coincides with the PRL 1992 silicone-oil dish geometry; the mature cone's apparent radial law fits the linear dish law better (R^2 0.977) than the exponential law (R^2 0.899), and its lattice is not perfectly log-periodic (closure residual 2.2 bins), so G_emp = 0.031 is an effective, not a developmental, plastochron ratio",
        "transfer_boundary: The 'observed' per-regime divergence means in the reference table are regime-level readings of Douady & Couder (1992) Figs. 1-2 and text, not digitised data with uncertainties; the dish-regime RMSE of 0.141 deg should be read against that provenance" ;
    pk1:aristotelianEfficientCause "4. Polar Auxin & Turgor Stress" ;
    pk1:aristotelianMegistonGenos "III. Phyta (Embryophyta)" ;
    pk1:aristotelianPoionForm "Spirals, Veins & Puzzle Cells" ;
    pk1:aristotelianPosonLaw "Golden Angle / Auxin Flux" ;
    pk1:aristotelianSubalternClass "Angiospermae & Gymnospermae" ;
    pk1:biologicalGenus "Helianthus" ;
    pk1:context "script(s): https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/1992-douady-magnetic-drop-phyllotaxis.py; output: docs/media/magnetic_drop_phyllotaxis_comparison.png; organism: Pinus sp. conifer seed cone & botanical shoot apical meristem (SAM); checkpoint commit: https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/commit/d58a084; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.16.3, matplotlib 3.10.7, Pillow 12.0.0; spec_fingerprint: 045b0921b1b4726ce33d0ec3190a3812d349153acf150593c5bf6c01da8f1e43; artifact_sha256: 09cbec33b6c20133934e29b9b7d5f3a8061d3f6cb4e1ddb93832f9db58f2db6d; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/magnetic_drop_phyllotaxis/conifer_cone_specimen.jpg=7bcb68e856d4db53..., datasets/magnetic_drop_phyllotaxis/magnetic_drop_phyllotaxis_reference.json=9ae33106a0fea23f..., datasets/magnetic_drop_phyllotaxis/paper_citations.bib=2c3aa1ec0e4c53de...}; supersedes_audit_id: 2026-10-19-magnetic-drop-phyllotaxis-audit-v2; claim_boundary: [reported_in_source: Douady & Couder (1992) Phys. Rev. Lett. 68:2098-2101 iterative magnetic-dipole repulsion energy E(phi) = sum_{k>=1} d_k(phi, phi_{n-k})^{-3} on a circular rim r = R_0 with linear dish advection r_k = R_0(1 + kG) controlled by the plastochron ratio G = V T / R_0; Figs. 1-2 dish regimes (1,1), (2,3), (3,5), (5,8), (8,13) and a metastable Lucas (4,7) | Douady & Couder (1992) Fig. 3 & (1996) J. Theor. Biol. 178:255-274 Secs. 3-4: supercritical (1,1)->(1,2) pitchfork of the iterated map, imperfect pitchfork cascade along the Fibonacci branch -> 137.508 deg, disconnected Lucas branch -> 99.502 deg, and nearest-neighbour contact parastichies on the van Iterson lattice; reconstructed_in_script: Exact static Hessian fold (G_fold = 0.773484 exp / 2.514560 lin) AND dynamical pitchfork (G_c1 = 0.859019 exp full chain / 3.631432 lin 2-drop) roots, the EMERGENT threshold of the unclamped iterated map (G_c1^emp = 0.8595 by bisection), the regular-spiral zero-force locus F(G, dphi) = 0, and adiabatic continuation along both Fibonacci (r = 0.99999, RMSE = 0.065 deg, contact pairs 9/10 table rows) and Lucas (RMSE = 0.141 deg) branches | Nearest-neighbour contact parastichy pairs on the true radii r_k = exp(kG) (Delaunay census kept as a secondary, biased extractor), memory-depth sweep N_mem in {1,2,3,5,8,13,21,45}, gamma in {1,3,5} universality, and simulated divergence / pair at the six tabulated dish regimes (RMSE 0.141 deg, 6/6 pairs) | Reciprocal-lattice inversion m*alpha + omega_m*G = 2*pi*j_m of the sub-bin (5, 8) log-polar FFT peaks of `conifer_cone_specimen.jpg` giving alpha_emp = 138.03 deg and G_emp = 0.0308, validated on a synthetic log-polar image of the simulated G = 0.06 lattice (0.014 deg / 0.06 % recovery error); transfer_boundary: Exponential meristem advection r_k = R_0 exp(kG) is displayed in the log-radial projection rho = 1 + ln(r/R_0) = 1 + kG, which coincides with the PRL 1992 silicone-oil dish geometry; the mature cone's apparent radial law fits the linear dish law better (R^2 0.977) than the exponential law (R^2 0.899), and its lattice is not perfectly log-periodic (closure residual 2.2 bins), so G_emp = 0.031 is an effective, not a developmental, plastochron ratio | The 'observed' per-regime divergence means in the reference table are regime-level readings of Douady & Couder (1992) Figs. 1-2 and text, not digitised data with uncertainties; the dish-regime RMSE of 0.141 deg should be read against that provenance; does_not_claim: Subcellular PIN1 polar auxin efflux carrier trafficking or continuous reaction-diffusion PDE dynamics on the meristem (Slot 033 Jönsson et al. 2006 / Smith et al. 2006); 3D photogrammetric or micro-CT cone reconstruction (the specimen analysis is a single 2D apical photograph of a 3D cone); a scale-level segmentation of the cone (the DoG detections over-count by ~2x and are not used at lattice level)]; other sources: Mathematische und mikroskopisch-anatomische Studien über Blattstellungen, nebst Betrachtungen über den Schalenbau der Miliolinen <https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/bibliography/9466>" ;
    pk1:derivedFromPaper <https://doi.org/10.1006/jtbi.1996.0024>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1006/jtbi.1996.0025>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevLett.68.2098>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1209/0295-5075/14/6/006> ;
    pk1:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-douady-magnetic-drop-phyllotaxis-code-traceability>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-douady-magnetic-drop-phyllotaxis-model-fidelity>,
