<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-douady-magnetic-drop-phyllotaxis-code-traceability> a pk1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Douady & Couder (1992, 1996) self-organized magnetic-drop phyllotaxis & imperfect pitchfork cascade — Code-to-model traceability: 91/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "The module docstring (L1-93) maps every section, including the Pass 3 additions, to PRL 1992 Eqs. (1)-(3) and Fig. 3, JTB 1996 Part I Secs. 2-4, Levitov (1991) and Lean 4 Theorems 1-5; each new function documents its equation and the v2 defect it replaces (`measure_emergent_pitchfork_threshold`, `extract_contact_parastichy_pair`, `log_polar_spiral_spectrum`, `invert_reciprocal_lattice_peaks`), and the inline comments at the remediated sites name the removed clamps and the clipped g_vis. Deductions: the dynamical discriminant S_dyn is attributed to 'JTB 1996 Part I Sec. 3.1' without an equation number, and the k-weighting is derived in-house rather than quoted (L283-297) (-4); the reciprocal-lattice relation is attributed to 'Sec. 4 van Iterson lattice' generically (L902-915) (-2); Row B's log-radial projection is justified in a comment but not tied to a specific D&C figure convention (L672-676) (-2); panel-building code (L1215-1575) cites figures only in titles (-1)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-code-traceability> ;
    pk1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/code-traceability" ;
    pk1:evidenceAgainst "1992-douady-magnetic-drop-phyllotaxis.py L283–L297: dynamical_pitchfork_discriminant_sum docstring cites JTB 1996 Part I Sec. 3.1 but the derivation is in-house (no equation number) <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/1992-douady-magnetic-drop-phyllotaxis.py#L283-L297>" ;
    pk1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-douady-magnetic-drop-phyllotaxis-code-traceability-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-douady-magnetic-drop-phyllotaxis-code-traceability-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-douady-magnetic-drop-phyllotaxis-code-traceability-3> ;
    pk1:hasScore 9.1e-01 ;
    pk1:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-douady-magnetic-drop-phyllotaxis-model-fidelity> a pk1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Douady & Couder (1992, 1996) self-organized magnetic-drop phyllotaxis & imperfect pitchfork cascade — Model fidelity to source: 92/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "The iterated rule phi_n = argmin E(phi) with E = sum_k d_k^{-gamma}, both advection laws, and the exact chord distance (L172-256) are Douady & Couder's Eqs. (1)-(3). Pass 3 removed the three hard-coded 180-deg short-circuits so the bifurcation is emergent (L347-398, L446-454, L722-742) and the measured threshold agrees with the analytic root of S_dyn(G) to 4.5e-4 (self-test 3); the two-drop integer form of S_dyn is machine-checked (Lean 4 Theorem 4, D(4,7) = -12646 < 0 < C(4,7) = 27687) and proves the static-fold / dynamical-threshold gap that v2 conflated in its measurement names. Contact parastichies now follow the authors' nearest-neighbour definition on the true radii (L539-577, L665-689). Deductions: the spiral branches of the equilibrium diagram are still labelled stable/unstable by the static Hessian sign while the 180-deg branch uses the dynamical criterion, a mixed criterion (L446-476) (-3); the memory depth N_mem = 45 is an ad-hoc truncation rather than the dish exit radius R_max/R_0 = 8 of the experiment (L610-620) (-2); the emergent threshold carries a +4.5e-4 finite-iteration bias (160 iterations, 0.5 deg criterion) that is tolerated rather than extrapolated (L347-398) (-1); the Delaunay census is kept as a secondary extractor although it disagrees with the contact pair at four transition rows (-2)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-model-fidelity> ;
    pk1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/model-fidelity" ;
    pk1:evidenceAgainst "1992-douady-magnetic-drop-phyllotaxis.py L446–L476: Equilibrium diagram: 180-deg branch stability from sign of S_dyn (computed), spiral branches still from the static Hessian sign — mixed criterion <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/1992-douady-magnetic-drop-phyllotaxis.py#L446-L476>" ;
    pk1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-douady-magnetic-drop-phyllotaxis-model-fidelity-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-douady-magnetic-drop-phyllotaxis-model-fidelity-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-douady-magnetic-drop-phyllotaxis-model-fidelity-3>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-douady-magnetic-drop-phyllotaxis-model-fidelity-4>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-douady-magnetic-drop-phyllotaxis-model-fidelity-5>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-douady-magnetic-drop-phyllotaxis-model-fidelity-6> ;
    pk1:hasScore 9.2e-01 ;
    pk1:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-douady-magnetic-drop-phyllotaxis-morphometric-validation> a pk1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Douady & Couder (1992, 1996) self-organized magnetic-drop phyllotaxis & imperfect pitchfork cascade — Morphometric validation: 89/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Eighteen measurements (L1581-1738) now carry provenance-tagged references: Fibonacci branch r = 0.99999 / RMSE 0.065 deg against the 10 benchmark rows with 9/10 contact pairs; Lucas 101.43 deg at the G = 0.10 table row (v2 compared G = 0.11 to the asymptote); static fold and dynamical G_c1 separated, with the analytic root checked against the emergent threshold; dish-regime RMSE 0.141 deg and 6/6 pairs; N_mem convergence index; and three specimen-level morphometrics — alpha_emp = 138.03 deg vs 137.508, G_emp = 0.0308 vs the 0.06 model regime, and the linear-vs-exponential radial-law R^2 gap — plus the disclosed negative result that radius-ranked detections give resultant R = 0.137. Deductions: the dish-regime 'observed' divergences are regime-level readings of PRL Figs. 1-2 with no uncertainties, so that RMSE is a weak validation (-4); the reference for the specimen's G is the model's own (5,8) regime value, and the measured 0.031 differs from it by 2x because the cone's radial law is linear, which is explained but not resolved (-3); the Voronoi CV reference is the theoretical 0 of a perfect lattice, not a measured value (-2); only one specimen contributes empirical morphometrics (-2)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-morphometric-validation> ;
    pk1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/morphometric-validation" ;
    pk1:evidenceAgainst "1992-douady-magnetic-drop-phyllotaxis.py L1668–L1674: ferrofluid_experiment_divergence_rmse_deg compares against table values whose provenance is a figure reading without uncertainties <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/1992-douady-magnetic-drop-phyllotaxis.py#L1668-L1674>" ;
    pk1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-douady-magnetic-drop-phyllotaxis-measurement-conifer-cone-lattice-divergence-angle-deg>,
